Method and preservation
-----------------------

  A blob-filtered sparse Git clone was deepened to retain BASE and every
  intervening commit. Pristine BASE and NEW archives were compared with a
  saved dirty LOCAL snapshot. No local implementation was discarded as
  upstream-equivalent. The six ISO headers, tests, ABI additions and manuals
  remain maintained implementations in this tree.

  Atomics and typed bit functions remain in libc (local version 104.1).
  The 25 C11 Threads functions were moved to their correct libpthread
  provider (local version 28.2; upstream 28.1). Consumers of the earlier
  local Threads extension must relink with -pthread. Historical upstream
  exports and public structure layouts are unchanged.

Verification before advancing NEW
--------------------------------

  patch contains 35 added and 18 modified source-relative files against NEW.
  It was applied to a fresh NEW archive without offsets, fuzz or rejects.
  All 3239 imported final paths matched the reconstruction byte-for-byte,
  including path sets, symlink targets and Git executable modes. No source
  added-line whitespace defects were found. The patch excludes host tests,
  reports and provenance metadata. No compiler or project runtime test was
  invoked during this synchronization; native builds/linking remain pending.

